            <b>name</b>, <b>version</b>, <b>features</b> and <b>usage</b> for every endpoint.
            CORS is wide open — <code>access-control-allow-origin: *</code> with <code>GET, HEAD, OPTIONS</code> —
            so it can be called straight from the browser, <b>no Worker proxy needed</b>.
